1
00:00:52,511 --> 00:00:53,345
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS,
INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

2
00:00:53,471 --> 00:00:54,305
ARE FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:54,430 --> 00:00:55,264
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY
UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

4
00:00:55,473 --> 00:00:56,348
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED
SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

5
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:09,361
I…

6
00:01:10,237 --> 00:01:11,864
kissed this man.

7
00:01:41,727 --> 00:01:43,103
YEONG-DO

8
00:01:44,563 --> 00:01:45,397
What's up?

9
00:01:45,523 --> 00:01:46,982
Namgung!

10
00:01:47,107 --> 00:01:48,567
Come to the karaoke.

11
00:01:48,692 --> 00:01:50,152
Get over here right now!

12
00:01:50,277 --> 00:01:52,488
-What are you doing?
-Let go of me!

13
00:01:52,613 --> 00:01:53,447
Punk!

14
00:01:54,365 --> 00:01:56,158
-What the heck?
-I'm so sorry.

15
00:01:56,283 --> 00:01:57,117
I apologize.

16
00:01:59,370 --> 00:02:01,580
I'm going crazy. I can't stop him now.

17
00:02:01,705 --> 00:02:02,998
-Get here now!
-Gosh.

18
00:02:05,459 --> 00:02:07,336
Hang on. I'll be right there.

19
00:02:17,596 --> 00:02:19,139
I don't know what you mean.

20
00:02:19,265 --> 00:02:21,058
Were you dreaming or something?

21
00:02:24,436 --> 00:02:25,771
You don't remember?

22
00:02:25,896 --> 00:02:28,691
I tend to black out when I drink.

23
00:02:30,526 --> 00:02:32,987
If I made a mistake, I apologize.

24
00:02:33,737 --> 00:02:36,782
It didn't mean anything, so don't worry…

25
00:02:53,591 --> 00:02:54,967
You really forgot?

26
00:02:58,929 --> 00:02:59,972
I don't think so.

27
00:03:00,556 --> 00:03:02,850
You look like you remember everything.

28
00:03:08,981 --> 00:03:10,733
"I'll let you quit directing."

29
00:03:13,402 --> 00:03:16,196
"I can do what your boyfriend

30
00:03:18,157 --> 00:03:19,575
can never do for you."

31
00:03:22,912 --> 00:03:24,204
Well?

32
00:03:26,916 --> 00:03:28,334
Is it coming back to you?

33
00:03:32,379 --> 00:03:33,923
I know you're confused.

34
00:03:34,632 --> 00:03:37,259
I came here because I'm just as confused.

35
00:03:39,261 --> 00:03:41,180
So I want to make a proposal.

36
00:03:43,265 --> 00:03:44,975
Let's have some fun for a bit.

37
00:03:46,143 --> 00:03:48,354
For you, a fling before marriage.

38
00:03:48,479 --> 00:03:50,606
And for me, just enough entertainment

39
00:03:52,399 --> 00:03:53,734
until I lose interest.

40
00:03:53,859 --> 00:03:55,945
We'll keep it at that.

41
00:03:57,821 --> 00:03:58,697
How about it?

42
00:04:01,408 --> 00:04:02,743
What do you think?

43
00:04:04,203 --> 00:04:05,746
-It wouldn't be too bad--
-You jerk!

44
00:04:05,871 --> 00:04:06,789
Hey!

45
00:04:16,507 --> 00:04:18,133
I regret what happened

46
00:04:18,258 --> 00:04:21,845
so much that I could die.

47
00:04:21,971 --> 00:04:23,097
So please,

48
00:04:23,722 --> 00:04:25,891
stay out of my sight.

49
00:04:26,433 --> 00:04:28,310
Please, please.

50
00:04:28,852 --> 00:04:30,104
I'm begging you.

51
00:04:30,688 --> 00:04:31,522
Please.

52
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:21,321
HONDURAS KARAOKE

53
00:05:27,119 --> 00:05:28,162
The watch.

54
00:05:28,829 --> 00:05:31,331
That damn watch he wears every single day.

55
00:05:31,915 --> 00:05:33,542
All this fuss over that watch.

56
00:05:33,667 --> 00:05:35,294
He's completely lost it.

57
00:05:35,419 --> 00:05:37,838
He tore up the house,
the salon, and now here.

58
00:05:38,505 --> 00:05:40,674
Good thing Mom is on a trip.

59
00:05:40,799 --> 00:05:42,718
Or she would've collapsed again.

60
00:05:51,643 --> 00:05:53,645
You were wearing it until yesterday.

61
00:05:55,856 --> 00:05:58,567
Yes, I was.

62
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:01,987
I don't know. It just disappeared.

63
00:06:02,696 --> 00:06:04,907
It's not like Bo-ra bought it for you.

64
00:06:05,032 --> 00:06:07,868
You got it when you joined
the Gyenam City team.

65
00:06:07,993 --> 00:06:09,244
Yeong-do.

66
00:06:10,704 --> 00:06:12,873
How long are you going to live like this?

67
00:06:12,998 --> 00:06:17,127
Do we have to keep walking on eggshells
every time you flip out like this?

68
00:06:19,463 --> 00:06:20,923
Bo-ra's ashes are in it.

69
00:06:27,805 --> 00:06:29,139
Bo-ra's ashes

70
00:06:30,390 --> 00:06:32,267
are inside the watch.

71
00:06:52,913 --> 00:06:54,289
-Hey!
-Huh?

72
00:06:58,669 --> 00:07:00,212
No, wait…

73
00:07:00,337 --> 00:07:01,421
-Follow me.
-Wait.

74
00:07:01,547 --> 00:07:04,383
-Wait a minute!
-Come here.

75
00:07:09,096 --> 00:07:10,139
Well…

76
00:07:11,598 --> 00:07:12,558
There's this

77
00:07:13,225 --> 00:07:15,310
challenge called "'99 Again"

78
00:07:16,895 --> 00:07:18,438
that's trending.

79
00:07:20,399 --> 00:07:22,317
So I borrowed Dad's suit,

80
00:07:23,569 --> 00:07:25,195
but it felt incomplete.

81
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:27,739
Then I saw you sleeping,

82
00:07:28,949 --> 00:07:30,576
and I saw the watch.

83
00:07:31,410 --> 00:07:33,328
It looked so old and vintage,

84
00:07:35,164 --> 00:07:39,209
so I just wanted to wear it for a bit
and then put it back.

85
00:07:42,921 --> 00:07:45,507
So where is it? Where's the watch now?

86
00:07:45,632 --> 00:07:48,635
Hey, yelling at him won't solve anything.

87
00:07:49,636 --> 00:07:52,222
Lee Sang-su, answer me straight.

88
00:07:54,349 --> 00:07:55,976
You lost the watch, didn't you?

89
00:07:59,396 --> 00:08:02,024
No, I mean…

90
00:08:02,858 --> 00:08:05,861
I had it on when I was filming,

91
00:08:08,530 --> 00:08:11,491
but then it suddenly disappeared.
I was scared--

92
00:08:11,617 --> 00:08:12,659
Hey!

93
00:08:15,746 --> 00:08:17,164
Why are you yelling at me?

94
00:08:18,207 --> 00:08:20,584
Why are you crying? Stop crying!

95
00:08:22,377 --> 00:08:23,754
You, too. Calm down.

96
00:08:23,879 --> 00:08:26,006
He can't speak if you yell at him.

97
00:08:26,131 --> 00:08:27,883
Yeong-do, if I don't find that watch,

98
00:08:28,592 --> 00:08:29,968
I won't let this go.

99
00:08:31,386 --> 00:08:32,888
I'm done with you two.

100
00:08:33,013 --> 00:08:33,972
Hey.

101
00:08:34,097 --> 00:08:36,683
You're saying that to your brother
over some watch?

102
00:08:39,436 --> 00:08:40,312
"Some watch"?

103
00:08:43,941 --> 00:08:45,275
Both of you, stop.

104
00:08:46,109 --> 00:08:48,237
Fighting like this won't solve anything.

105
00:08:49,321 --> 00:08:50,405
Sang-su, stop crying.

106
00:08:52,449 --> 00:08:53,951
It's getting late.

107
00:08:54,576 --> 00:08:56,536
Let's check the stream
first thing tomorrow.

108
00:08:57,246 --> 00:09:00,290
Sang-su, send me all the footage.

109
00:09:00,415 --> 00:09:02,793
We need the exact spot
to narrow the search.

110
00:09:14,596 --> 00:09:17,432
Stop crying. What are you even crying for?

111
00:09:18,225 --> 00:09:20,978
What if Aunt Bo-ra comes for me?

112
00:09:21,103 --> 00:09:22,646
I'm scared.

113
00:09:22,771 --> 00:09:24,189
That won't happen.

114
00:09:24,314 --> 00:09:26,942
He said Aunt Bo-ra's ashes
were in the watch.

115
00:09:27,067 --> 00:09:28,443
I had no idea.

116
00:09:28,986 --> 00:09:31,154
I wore it and danced to "Boom Boom Boom."

117
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:33,365
I even did Bollywood dances.

118
00:09:33,490 --> 00:09:34,658
That Bo-ra…

119
00:09:35,325 --> 00:09:37,619
She never visited Wan-do in four years.

120
00:09:38,287 --> 00:09:39,246
Don't worry.

121
00:09:39,830 --> 00:09:42,457
But since I lost the watch,

122
00:09:43,083 --> 00:09:44,501
she might come to punish me.

123
00:09:44,626 --> 00:09:47,087
Then tell her to go see your uncle.

124
00:09:56,013 --> 00:09:56,847
Actually, no.

125
00:09:59,349 --> 00:10:00,559
Sang-su.

126
00:10:01,643 --> 00:10:03,645
If Aunt Bo-ra pays you a visit,

127
00:10:04,354 --> 00:10:06,189
you have to beg her

128
00:10:06,857 --> 00:10:08,442
not to go see your uncle.

129
00:10:09,276 --> 00:10:10,110
What?

130
00:10:11,903 --> 00:10:13,030
No way.

131
00:10:13,822 --> 00:10:15,907
Why would you say that?

132
00:10:16,033 --> 00:10:17,409
I'm scared!

133
00:10:17,534 --> 00:10:19,536
Stop crying and tell her exactly this.

134
00:10:21,038 --> 00:10:23,457
Tell her to stay away from Wan-do.

135
00:10:23,582 --> 00:10:25,334
To please let him live in peace.

136
00:10:26,460 --> 00:10:28,503
To please just leave him alone.

137
00:10:29,171 --> 00:10:31,631
Why are you doing this? It's scary.

138
00:10:35,260 --> 00:10:36,720
Your mom's side is Catholic.

139
00:10:37,637 --> 00:10:39,931
We have six priests in the family.

140
00:10:41,141 --> 00:10:42,684
You'll be fine, Gabriel.

141
00:10:44,311 --> 00:10:46,396
Look, I'm sorry!

142
00:10:47,064 --> 00:10:48,607
Stop it!

143
00:10:48,732 --> 00:10:50,025
Come on, let's go.

144
00:10:52,527 --> 00:10:53,945
Gabriel…

145
00:11:18,929 --> 00:11:19,971
Mi-do, you asleep?

146
00:11:21,681 --> 00:11:23,725
You never go to sleep before 2 a.m.

147
00:11:27,521 --> 00:11:29,689
I'm completely done with that woman.

148
00:11:31,566 --> 00:11:33,693
I'll never see her again.

149
00:11:38,949 --> 00:11:40,075
Hey, are you crying?

150
00:11:45,038 --> 00:11:46,957
Why are you crying? You're making me sad.

151
00:11:51,545 --> 00:11:54,756
Namgung, what happened to your face?

152
00:11:54,881 --> 00:11:55,924
Did she do that?

153
00:12:01,304 --> 00:12:02,722
It's all over now.

154
00:12:04,850 --> 00:12:07,811
You won't have to worry
about this ever again.

155
00:12:11,231 --> 00:12:12,607
So please stop crying.

156
00:12:15,819 --> 00:12:17,654
Don't cry.

157
00:12:29,249 --> 00:12:35,130
6. WHO IS OUR BEST HERO?

158
00:12:36,339 --> 00:12:37,674
Take a look at this.

159
00:12:39,009 --> 00:12:40,802
I trusted her to close up,

160
00:12:40,927 --> 00:12:44,389
but she was secretly
taking customers late at night.

161
00:12:44,514 --> 00:12:46,057
Unbelievable.

162
00:12:56,776 --> 00:12:58,069
What are you doing?

163
00:12:58,195 --> 00:13:00,447
I was going to call the cops,

164
00:13:00,572 --> 00:13:03,241
but I called the family contact
on your resume first.

165
00:13:03,366 --> 00:13:04,326
So ungrateful.

166
00:13:07,287 --> 00:13:08,246
What will you do?

167
00:13:09,039 --> 00:13:10,165
Are you going to pay

168
00:13:11,541 --> 00:13:12,751
3.2 million won?

169
00:13:13,835 --> 00:13:14,878
She's not family.

170
00:13:16,630 --> 00:13:17,672
She's a friend.

171
00:13:17,797 --> 00:13:19,090
Talk to me.

172
00:13:21,843 --> 00:13:22,844
Call the cops.

173
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:28,725
That'll teach her a lesson.

174
00:13:39,027 --> 00:13:40,362
ATM

175
00:13:40,487 --> 00:13:43,949
Please take your card.
Cash will be dispensed.

176
00:13:44,074 --> 00:13:45,492
Please take your cash.

177
00:13:45,617 --> 00:13:47,244
CASH DISPENSER

178
00:13:49,204 --> 00:13:51,331
Thank you for your transaction.
Have a nice day.

179
00:13:55,377 --> 00:13:56,211
Su-a.

180
00:14:00,298 --> 00:14:01,967
The salon owner does this a lot.

181
00:14:02,801 --> 00:14:04,844
We fought over my days off.

182
00:14:04,970 --> 00:14:07,055
She promised to help with my training,

183
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:08,848
then she treated me like a thief.

184
00:14:12,602 --> 00:14:13,436
You…

185
00:14:17,357 --> 00:14:18,858
don't believe me, do you?

186
00:14:19,568 --> 00:14:20,652
Then earn my trust.

187
00:14:22,028 --> 00:14:23,154
With the CCTV footage,

188
00:14:23,280 --> 00:14:25,615
your online post, the contract,

189
00:14:25,740 --> 00:14:28,243
and how you ignored the owner's calls,

190
00:14:29,202 --> 00:14:30,829
how can I trust you?

191
00:14:46,845 --> 00:14:47,679
HYDROCOLLOID BANDAGE

192
00:14:49,848 --> 00:14:51,933
Don't use the bandage on your face.

193
00:14:52,934 --> 00:14:54,686
It'll scar your pretty face.

194
00:14:55,979 --> 00:14:59,816
I'll get my things tomorrow
when you go to work.

195
00:14:59,941 --> 00:15:01,651
I'll pay you back soon, too.

196
00:15:06,740 --> 00:15:08,241
Sorry for bothering you.

197
00:15:09,618 --> 00:15:10,577
I won't ever…

198
00:15:11,870 --> 00:15:13,121
contact you again.

199
00:15:47,238 --> 00:15:50,992
Make sure you eat.
Eat everything even if you're not hungry.

200
00:15:51,117 --> 00:15:52,452
And take your red ginseng.

201
00:16:10,345 --> 00:16:12,347
Mi-do has been acting weird.

202
00:16:14,808 --> 00:16:15,684
Why?

203
00:16:15,809 --> 00:16:17,102
Because you met your mom?

204
00:16:17,227 --> 00:16:19,938
Still? That was days ago.

205
00:16:20,605 --> 00:16:22,065
Yes, but…

206
00:16:30,240 --> 00:16:31,074
What's wrong?

207
00:16:32,325 --> 00:16:33,827
Why are you crying?

208
00:16:33,952 --> 00:16:35,203
Looks good.

209
00:16:40,458 --> 00:16:41,876
What's wrong, Mi-do?

210
00:16:45,755 --> 00:16:47,173
Why do you keep crying?

211
00:17:02,939 --> 00:17:05,442
Mi-do cries
whenever she sees me these days.

212
00:17:05,567 --> 00:17:06,526
She just

213
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:09,487
keeps crying.

214
00:17:09,612 --> 00:17:11,114
Is she going through menopause?

215
00:17:12,157 --> 00:17:14,117
Lots of women get it in their thirties.

216
00:17:14,242 --> 00:17:15,118
Come on.

217
00:17:16,202 --> 00:17:17,412
Don't be ridiculous.

218
00:17:17,537 --> 00:17:18,955
How else can you explain it?

219
00:17:19,664 --> 00:17:22,333
Why would a tough girl like her
cry every day?

220
00:17:23,001 --> 00:17:25,670
You were crying every day too
after the divorce. Remember?

221
00:17:25,795 --> 00:17:27,964
Why would you bring that up now?

222
00:17:29,215 --> 00:17:30,383
What about you?

223
00:17:31,259 --> 00:17:32,385
Sulking because of your nephew.

224
00:17:33,595 --> 00:17:35,597
I heard you ignored
Sang-su's text last night.

225
00:17:35,722 --> 00:17:37,390
That kid…

226
00:17:37,515 --> 00:17:39,058
Tell him to stay away.

227
00:17:39,809 --> 00:17:41,811
Hey, man, he's 14 years old.

228
00:17:41,936 --> 00:17:44,105
Aren't embarrassed
to be fighting with a kid?

229
00:17:44,230 --> 00:17:45,148
What about you?

230
00:17:45,774 --> 00:17:47,984
You fight with that kid.
Aren't you embarrassed?

231
00:17:48,109 --> 00:17:50,111
Oh, you little punk.

232
00:17:57,535 --> 00:17:58,411
Keep going.

233
00:17:58,536 --> 00:18:00,789
Why don't you keep going?

234
00:18:00,914 --> 00:18:02,415
Why don't you do it right?

235
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:04,000
Don't half-ass it.

236
00:18:04,667 --> 00:18:07,504
Should I call Ms. Ma, Mi-do,
and Sang-su, all of them?

237
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:11,466
Jeez, seriously.

238
00:18:11,591 --> 00:18:12,884
You guys fight every day.

239
00:18:21,601 --> 00:18:23,144
-Where is it?
-Namgung.

240
00:18:24,979 --> 00:18:25,814
Are you…

241
00:18:27,065 --> 00:18:27,982
okay?

242
00:18:28,107 --> 00:18:30,026
What? I can't hear you.

243
00:18:30,777 --> 00:18:31,736
I mean…

244
00:18:34,405 --> 00:18:36,241
you met with your mom.

245
00:18:41,287 --> 00:18:42,580
Right. Ho.

246
00:18:43,164 --> 00:18:43,998
Are you okay?

247
00:18:44,123 --> 00:18:46,125
I heard she caused trouble again.

248
00:18:47,085 --> 00:18:47,961
Nothing serious, right?

249
00:18:48,086 --> 00:18:49,254
Of course it's serious.

250
00:18:51,589 --> 00:18:54,384
A warrant was issued,
and she's in a detention center.

251
00:18:54,926 --> 00:18:55,844
Hey!

252
00:18:57,762 --> 00:18:59,848
-You scared me.
-If that happened,

253
00:18:59,973 --> 00:19:01,474
you should've told us right away.

254
00:19:01,599 --> 00:19:03,268
You just said you saw her,

255
00:19:03,393 --> 00:19:05,645
so I thought
it was just about money again.

256
00:19:06,980 --> 00:19:08,523
Why are you always like this?

257
00:19:08,648 --> 00:19:09,816
Does Mi-do know?

258
00:19:09,941 --> 00:19:12,110
She's been acting weird because of you.

259
00:19:12,235 --> 00:19:13,820
Why are you like this?

260
00:19:13,945 --> 00:19:15,655
Always telling us when it's over.

261
00:19:15,780 --> 00:19:17,907
Didn't I tell you never to do that again?

262
00:19:18,032 --> 00:19:19,742
Stop doing that.

263
00:19:19,868 --> 00:19:21,744
We're friends. It really hurts.

264
00:19:24,038 --> 00:19:26,040
I'd feel so pathetic telling you.

265
00:19:31,713 --> 00:19:34,048
The fact that a woman like her is my mom

266
00:19:36,050 --> 00:19:38,261
is just so pathetic and embarrassing.

267
00:19:41,723 --> 00:19:43,141
I feel so pathetic and embarrassed

268
00:19:45,226 --> 00:19:47,186
in front of you and Wan-do,

269
00:19:48,313 --> 00:19:49,939
and especially in front of Mi-do.

270
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:53,818
So I couldn't tell you.

271
00:19:55,028 --> 00:19:55,945
I'm sorry.

272
00:19:58,740 --> 00:19:59,741
Oh, jeez.

273
00:20:02,076 --> 00:20:02,911
Goodness.

274
00:20:05,747 --> 00:20:07,373
Say that one more time.

275
00:20:07,498 --> 00:20:08,750
I'll seriously get mad.

276
00:20:08,875 --> 00:20:11,961
Yes, I'll get mad, too!

277
00:20:13,463 --> 00:20:15,632
I was too embarrassed to tell you this,

278
00:20:16,299 --> 00:20:18,635
but in the last
civil service exam I failed,

279
00:20:18,760 --> 00:20:21,429
my average wasn't 55. It was 37.

280
00:20:22,263 --> 00:20:26,309
Yes, and I was too embarrassed
to say this too,

281
00:20:26,434 --> 00:20:28,061
but my driving test…

282
00:20:28,686 --> 00:20:32,607
I didn't fail four times.
I failed seven times.

283
00:20:38,279 --> 00:20:42,325
You took the civil service exam
for three straight years and got a 37?

284
00:20:43,868 --> 00:20:45,536
Are you even an athlete?

285
00:20:45,662 --> 00:20:48,665
How do you fail a driving test
seven times?

286
00:20:52,126 --> 00:20:54,337
That's hilarious, man.

287
00:20:54,462 --> 00:20:55,588
Hey, get that punk.

288
00:20:55,713 --> 00:20:57,715
-Hey!
-Get him!

289
00:20:57,840 --> 00:20:59,258
No!

290
00:20:59,384 --> 00:21:01,302
-Get him!
-Wait!

291
00:21:02,762 --> 00:21:04,764
Time out!

292
00:21:04,889 --> 00:21:05,807
Ouch!

293
00:21:07,642 --> 00:21:09,394
Hey, the watch!

294
00:21:09,519 --> 00:21:11,229
I won't fall for that twice, punk!

295
00:21:11,354 --> 00:21:14,273
No, I'm serious! Look!

296
00:21:39,674 --> 00:21:41,342
How many meters today?

297
00:21:45,013 --> 00:21:46,305
210 meters.

298
00:21:49,225 --> 00:21:51,144
Still so deep.

299
00:22:03,072 --> 00:22:05,116
When we scattered Bo-ra into the sea…

300
00:22:10,288 --> 00:22:12,623
something got caught in my hand.

301
00:22:16,669 --> 00:22:17,837
THE LATE BAEK BO-RA

302
00:22:18,880 --> 00:22:20,465
Bo-ra…

303
00:22:23,468 --> 00:22:27,305
No, Bo-ra!

304
00:23:16,145 --> 00:23:17,605
I'm really pathetic, aren't I?

305
00:23:51,180 --> 00:23:52,348
I regret what happened

306
00:23:53,182 --> 00:23:56,519
so much that I could die.

307
00:23:57,186 --> 00:23:59,397
Stay out of my sight.

308
00:24:04,443 --> 00:24:05,695
Damn it.

309
00:24:18,541 --> 00:24:20,835
Let's discuss the case
about the researcher in person.

310
00:24:20,960 --> 00:24:22,336
Not over the phone.

311
00:24:22,461 --> 00:24:24,255
The researcher isn't the issue.

312
00:24:24,380 --> 00:24:25,798
Didn't you hear about Jisang?

313
00:24:26,382 --> 00:24:28,634
Things are looking bad at Jisang.

314
00:24:29,260 --> 00:24:30,845
I think something went wrong.

315
00:24:30,970 --> 00:24:33,890
Last night, the cops
and the Financial Supervisory Service

316
00:24:34,015 --> 00:24:37,727
raided Line's accounting HQ
and seized all their servers.

317
00:24:37,852 --> 00:24:39,812
Didn't Mr. Seo tell you anything?

318
00:24:40,855 --> 00:24:41,689
Hello?

319
00:24:42,607 --> 00:24:44,108
Are you listening?

320
00:24:44,942 --> 00:24:46,652
Gosh, is he listening or not?

321
00:24:53,826 --> 00:24:56,579
Mr. Han, why don't you take a vacation?

322
00:24:58,122 --> 00:24:59,040
You know…

323
00:25:00,124 --> 00:25:02,793
you haven't had a break
since the Cheonsong Electronics case.

324
00:25:02,919 --> 00:25:05,171
Let Attorney Lee finish up Jisang's case.

325
00:25:05,296 --> 00:25:07,423
Get some fresh air for two weeks.

326
00:25:07,548 --> 00:25:09,342
We still have the appeal.

327
00:25:11,093 --> 00:25:12,553
I have to settle this.

328
00:25:14,222 --> 00:25:15,514
Jisang's cash flow

329
00:25:16,724 --> 00:25:19,894
will be cut off
once the damages claim is enforced.

330
00:25:20,019 --> 00:25:21,229
Mediation is the only option.

331
00:25:22,313 --> 00:25:24,482
Chairman Ko will accept it soon.

332
00:25:28,110 --> 00:25:30,988
I didn't expect to be sent off
empty-handed like this.

333
00:25:36,327 --> 00:25:37,161
What was that?

334
00:25:41,916 --> 00:25:43,584
You have no conscience.

335
00:25:44,377 --> 00:25:46,003
You worked me to the bone.

336
00:25:48,965 --> 00:25:51,842
You should at least get me
a business-class ticket.

337
00:25:55,638 --> 00:25:57,181
I'll get you first class.

338
00:25:57,974 --> 00:26:00,142
Just say the word. Where to?

339
00:26:04,063 --> 00:26:05,773
I don't want anywhere too hot.

340
00:26:08,234 --> 00:26:09,819
Or too humid.

341
00:26:24,250 --> 00:26:25,334
So I'm a dog?

342
00:26:25,459 --> 00:26:27,128
A lapdog, to be exact.

343
00:26:27,253 --> 00:26:30,047
A lapdog who could get dumped
by his master any second.

344
00:26:30,965 --> 00:26:32,008
Hi.

345
00:26:36,304 --> 00:26:39,849
This is a piece called a knight
in a game called chess.

346
00:26:40,641 --> 00:26:43,269
It's the most
unpredictable piece in chess.

347
00:26:44,186 --> 00:26:45,021
The knight.

348
00:26:46,564 --> 00:26:49,025
A rook can only move in straight lines,

349
00:26:49,150 --> 00:26:50,401
but not this one.

350
00:26:52,403 --> 00:26:54,864
Even when it seems completely blocked,

351
00:26:56,741 --> 00:26:58,492
it moves in an L-shape

352
00:26:59,702 --> 00:27:00,745
to create a chance.

353
00:27:01,537 --> 00:27:04,707
It may look like a dead end,
but it's not over.

354
00:27:04,832 --> 00:27:07,001
Even if it doesn't go straight,

355
00:27:07,960 --> 00:27:11,839
it can freely change the game
as it moves on the board.

356
00:27:12,882 --> 00:27:13,716
I'm here…

357
00:27:15,426 --> 00:27:16,761
to give you

358
00:27:17,553 --> 00:27:19,180
that chance right now.

359
00:27:21,057 --> 00:27:23,559
Whether you tell me the truth or not,

360
00:27:24,352 --> 00:27:26,270
I plan to make it happen.

361
00:27:27,772 --> 00:27:30,358
So trust me now,

362
00:27:32,401 --> 00:27:34,570
and tell me
what happened to you that night.

363
00:27:35,905 --> 00:27:37,031
Will you?

364
00:28:08,813 --> 00:28:10,189
Mi-do, are you up?

365
00:28:10,815 --> 00:28:11,690
Still not feeling well?

366
00:28:11,816 --> 00:28:12,650
MIDORI

367
00:28:12,775 --> 00:28:14,735
Want to get chicken feet
from Bongcheon later?

368
00:28:19,198 --> 00:28:20,491
46TH COHORT LEE MIN-GI: DID YOU SEE
THE JOB POST FOR THE POSITION IN FRANCE?

369
00:28:24,036 --> 00:28:26,330
Did you see the job post
for the position in France?

370
00:28:34,171 --> 00:28:37,341
What are you looking at so intently,
Mr. Namgung?

371
00:28:38,384 --> 00:28:40,177
EXPAT POSITION IN PARIS
CONFECTIONERY MARKETING & SALES

372
00:28:40,302 --> 00:28:41,762
Are you applying for it?

373
00:28:42,805 --> 00:28:45,266
I'm thinking about it.
The perks are pretty good.

374
00:28:45,391 --> 00:28:46,559
Wow, you traitor.

375
00:28:46,684 --> 00:28:48,352
What about our Spicy SweeTato Chips?

376
00:28:49,270 --> 00:28:52,356
I was going to bail if it didn't launch
by Q3 next year anyway.

377
00:28:52,481 --> 00:28:54,608
You're so bold when the boss is away.

378
00:28:54,733 --> 00:28:56,026
I'm telling on you.

379
00:28:57,069 --> 00:28:59,405
You probably wouldn't get it anyway.

380
00:29:00,573 --> 00:29:03,075
I heard about this from a friend in HR.

381
00:29:03,200 --> 00:29:04,702
They need a French speaker.

382
00:29:04,827 --> 00:29:06,245
I double-majored in French.

383
00:29:06,370 --> 00:29:07,246
What?

384
00:29:07,371 --> 00:29:08,747
My GPA was 4.3.

385
00:29:09,457 --> 00:29:11,625
I wiped the floor with the French majors.

386
00:29:12,460 --> 00:29:13,627
What?

387
00:29:13,752 --> 00:29:16,464
Why are you so fluent?
Why is your accent so good?

388
00:29:16,589 --> 00:29:19,008
-Are you--
-Are you really going?

389
00:29:19,133 --> 00:29:21,135
Why?

390
00:29:22,261 --> 00:29:23,637
Launching isn't the end.

391
00:29:23,762 --> 00:29:25,306
What about marketing? Pop-ups?

392
00:29:26,515 --> 00:29:30,144
Wow, were you always this irresponsible?

393
00:29:30,269 --> 00:29:31,937
Or is it because of ambition?

394
00:29:32,062 --> 00:29:35,232
Because expats
are first in line for promotions?

395
00:29:35,900 --> 00:29:37,818
Or is it the salary?

396
00:29:37,943 --> 00:29:40,613
If not that,
is it the MBA tuition support?

397
00:29:40,738 --> 00:29:42,281
Is it because of that?

398
00:29:45,659 --> 00:29:47,369
It's on my girlfriend's bucket list.

399
00:29:53,042 --> 00:29:56,795
My girlfriend has always
wanted to live in Paris.

400
00:29:57,630 --> 00:29:58,964
She's been down lately.

401
00:29:59,089 --> 00:30:01,592
Two years there
would be a nice change of pace.

402
00:30:02,760 --> 00:30:04,053
Will the competition be tough?

403
00:30:06,013 --> 00:30:07,264
Mr. Namgung.

404
00:30:08,182 --> 00:30:09,725
Are you getting married?

405
00:30:10,392 --> 00:30:12,061
You are, right?

406
00:30:12,895 --> 00:30:14,813
Wow, congratulations!

407
00:30:15,481 --> 00:30:16,607
Pretend you don't know.

408
00:30:16,732 --> 00:30:19,443
If the boss knows I didn't tell him,
he'll pout for a week.

409
00:30:19,568 --> 00:30:23,072
You're finally off the market.

410
00:30:23,197 --> 00:30:25,032
Seriously, congratulations.

411
00:30:25,991 --> 00:30:28,661
Isn't your girlfriend your first love?

412
00:30:31,830 --> 00:30:33,832
You don't have an appointment.

413
00:30:34,917 --> 00:30:38,337
I'm asking because he won't answer!

414
00:30:38,462 --> 00:30:41,382
Assistant Manager Namgung Ho
with TF Snack Team 3!

415
00:30:41,507 --> 00:30:44,677
If you keep making a scene,
we'll have to call the police.

416
00:30:44,802 --> 00:30:46,345
Want to see a real scene?

417
00:30:46,470 --> 00:30:48,389
Just make one phone call!

418
00:30:48,514 --> 00:30:49,682
-You need to leave.
-What?

419
00:30:49,807 --> 00:30:51,058
-I warned you.
-Leave?

420
00:30:51,183 --> 00:30:52,226
-Leave where?
-Why?

421
00:30:52,351 --> 00:30:54,353
-Call the cops!
-Okay.

422
00:30:54,478 --> 00:30:56,480
-Get out.
-You want to do this?

423
00:30:56,605 --> 00:30:57,565
-Hit me.
-You punk!

424
00:31:03,737 --> 00:31:05,322
Well, look who it is.

425
00:31:05,447 --> 00:31:07,157
Our precious debtor.

426
00:31:08,534 --> 00:31:10,536
You're much more handsome in person.

427
00:31:11,704 --> 00:31:12,788
Nice to meet you.

428
00:31:16,208 --> 00:31:18,002
Let's take this outside.

429
00:31:24,091 --> 00:31:26,760
Namgung, I'm at a cafe near your office.

430
00:31:26,885 --> 00:31:29,013
I'll write here until you're off work.

431
00:31:29,138 --> 00:31:30,097
Let's get dinner.

432
00:31:30,222 --> 00:31:32,683
Did Mr. Namgung take out a private loan?

433
00:31:33,350 --> 00:31:35,185
No way.

434
00:31:35,311 --> 00:31:38,480
I worked with him at the pop-up.
He's definitely not like that.

435
00:31:38,606 --> 00:31:41,066
Then why would a loan shark come here?

436
00:31:41,191 --> 00:31:42,401
We all saw it.

437
00:31:42,526 --> 00:31:44,153
He must have his reasons.

438
00:31:44,278 --> 00:31:47,072
Come to think of it,
when Assistant Manager Gung was new,

439
00:31:47,197 --> 00:31:49,116
I heard something similar happened.

440
00:31:49,241 --> 00:31:50,117
What?

441
00:31:50,242 --> 00:31:53,203
He was the first rookie
to get his paycheck garnished.

442
00:31:53,329 --> 00:31:55,331
There was a lot of talk
in the finance team.

443
00:31:56,832 --> 00:31:58,000
I think I heard about that too.

444
00:31:58,125 --> 00:31:59,793
Was he gambling?

445
00:31:59,918 --> 00:32:02,254
Like sports betting or something?

446
00:32:03,130 --> 00:32:07,676
You know, those clean-cut guys
usually have dirty secrets.

447
00:32:07,801 --> 00:32:09,011
Knock it off.

448
00:32:09,595 --> 00:32:12,306
Don't gossip when you don't know anything.

449
00:32:12,973 --> 00:32:14,683
I'm embarrassed to be your coworker.

450
00:32:14,808 --> 00:32:17,311
Focus on your own work
instead of gossiping.

451
00:32:22,483 --> 00:32:24,693
-That scared me.
-Seriously.

452
00:32:27,196 --> 00:32:28,322
Excuse me.

453
00:32:34,411 --> 00:32:36,872
The person you are calling is unavailable.
Please leave a message…

454
00:32:37,414 --> 00:32:39,291
At what time did he leave with those guys?

455
00:32:39,416 --> 00:32:42,044
Less than 20 minutes ago.
I'm sure he's fine.

456
00:32:44,254 --> 00:32:46,548
If it was serious, we'd have called 911.

457
00:32:46,674 --> 00:32:48,008
He said not to worry.

458
00:32:48,133 --> 00:32:49,927
You still should've called 911.

459
00:32:50,052 --> 00:32:51,762
Anything could happen.

460
00:32:52,763 --> 00:32:54,640
You're worrying too much.

461
00:32:54,765 --> 00:32:56,975
In broad daylight in Seoul? What could…

462
00:32:57,101 --> 00:32:58,894
But what if something does happen?

463
00:32:59,645 --> 00:33:02,272
What if something happens to Namgung?

464
00:33:06,694 --> 00:33:08,404
Oh, I'm sorry.

465
00:33:09,029 --> 00:33:11,949
I shouldn't take it out on you.
I'm just so worried.

466
00:33:12,074 --> 00:33:13,575
I'm sorry. I really am.

467
00:33:28,465 --> 00:33:29,591
PROMISSORY NOTE
STANDARD LOAN AGREEMENT

468
00:33:29,717 --> 00:33:30,551
Your mother,

469
00:33:30,676 --> 00:33:32,636
Choi Hwa-young, borrowed 300 million won.

470
00:33:32,761 --> 00:33:34,722
You know she's in custody, right?

471
00:33:34,847 --> 00:33:37,141
She'll be short on the interest payment
starting this month,

472
00:33:37,266 --> 00:33:38,809
so we came a bit early.

473
00:33:39,476 --> 00:33:42,521
If you lent money to a con artist
without collateral,

474
00:33:43,772 --> 00:33:46,316
wasn't that a risk
you were willing to take?

475
00:33:48,485 --> 00:33:50,946
Who knew she'd blow it
before she even started?

476
00:33:51,780 --> 00:33:54,116
I hear you're the one who messed it up.

477
00:33:54,241 --> 00:33:56,034
Then you should take the fall.

478
00:33:56,160 --> 00:33:59,747
By the way, you know renouncing
your inheritance won't work, right?

479
00:33:59,872 --> 00:34:01,832
We don't care about the law--

480
00:34:03,167 --> 00:34:05,586
Seeing a guy like you
reminds me of someone.

481
00:34:06,628 --> 00:34:08,464
This is the tibialis posterior.

482
00:34:09,339 --> 00:34:10,507
-What?
-My biological father

483
00:34:10,632 --> 00:34:13,051
was supposedly great at cutting it.

484
00:34:13,802 --> 00:34:17,222
Guess he was a famous knifeman
in your line of work.

485
00:34:19,057 --> 00:34:21,727
He crippled a ton of people.

486
00:34:22,811 --> 00:34:23,937
Choi Hwa-young said

487
00:34:24,062 --> 00:34:27,816
it was creepy how he'd giggle
while he worked.

488
00:34:30,986 --> 00:34:32,321
Are you threatening me?

489
00:34:32,446 --> 00:34:33,947
It's not a threat.

490
00:34:34,072 --> 00:34:37,075
I'm just saying my blood is trash.

491
00:34:37,201 --> 00:34:40,204
Look, you think words like that
would make us flinch?

492
00:34:40,871 --> 00:34:43,123
-We've seen tons of guys--
-I'm sure you have.

493
00:34:45,250 --> 00:34:46,835
But I'm different.

494
00:34:49,838 --> 00:34:50,964
I'm very different.

495
00:34:53,217 --> 00:34:54,343
You probably know,

496
00:34:54,468 --> 00:34:56,637
but I only have one kidney.

497
00:34:57,221 --> 00:34:59,431
I'm not giving up my liver or eyes.

498
00:35:00,557 --> 00:35:03,060
And you'd better not mess with
the people around me.

499
00:35:05,604 --> 00:35:07,022
Who do you think you are?

500
00:35:08,148 --> 00:35:09,441
Why so confident?

501
00:35:10,234 --> 00:35:12,402
You have no idea what we can do.

502
00:35:12,528 --> 00:35:13,529
Sorry, but…

503
00:35:14,863 --> 00:35:16,949
I already died when I was seven,

504
00:35:19,952 --> 00:35:21,703
so I'm living on borrowed time.

505
00:35:25,707 --> 00:35:26,667
That's why…

506
00:35:30,087 --> 00:35:31,797
I'm not afraid of dying.

507
00:35:33,674 --> 00:35:35,092
Mess with me and see.

508
00:35:36,260 --> 00:35:38,220
I'll show you how crazy I can get.

509
00:35:47,396 --> 00:35:48,939
Excuse me!

510
00:35:53,360 --> 00:35:55,654
Seriously, congratulations.

511
00:35:55,779 --> 00:35:58,365
Isn't your girlfriend your first love?

512
00:36:00,033 --> 00:36:01,743
"First love…"

513
00:36:03,412 --> 00:36:05,205
is a bit too cheesy.

514
00:36:06,415 --> 00:36:08,500
If I had to describe her,

515
00:36:09,668 --> 00:36:10,878
maybe a hero?

516
00:36:12,963 --> 00:36:15,841
My girlfriend is really awesome.

517
00:36:17,426 --> 00:36:19,136
It's impossible

518
00:36:20,178 --> 00:36:21,847
for you not to…

519
00:36:26,310 --> 00:36:27,561
fall so hard for her.

520
00:36:32,024 --> 00:36:35,235
Lee Mi-do was
the greatest hero in my life.

521
00:36:43,994 --> 00:36:48,123
After I died at seven, she revived me
and then kept on saving me over and over.

522
00:36:48,248 --> 00:36:50,959
She's truly the greatest hero in my life.

523
00:36:51,627 --> 00:36:52,502
Die, you little shit!

524
00:36:53,837 --> 00:36:56,006
Damn you! My gosh.

525
00:36:57,925 --> 00:37:00,135
You little piece of shit.

526
00:37:06,350 --> 00:37:08,477
Namgung, are you okay?

527
00:37:09,144 --> 00:37:10,354
Namgung. Oh no.

528
00:37:11,855 --> 00:37:12,981
Are you all right?

529
00:37:19,446 --> 00:37:20,364
Mi-do.

530
00:37:24,409 --> 00:37:27,329
But since he's a minor,
he'll be released soon, right?

531
00:37:29,164 --> 00:37:30,832
Everything he said is a lie.

532
00:37:39,341 --> 00:37:40,842
Namgung Ho was taking his midterms

533
00:37:40,968 --> 00:37:43,053
during the time
the victim was texting them.

534
00:37:43,178 --> 00:37:46,014
The account is in Namgung Ho's name,
but Aunt Hwa-young used it.

535
00:37:47,140 --> 00:37:49,726
The evidence is all here. Please check it.

536
00:37:50,560 --> 00:37:51,478
Damn it.

537
00:37:53,063 --> 00:37:55,107
What are you smiling at?

538
00:37:55,232 --> 00:37:56,858
You almost went to juvie.

539
00:37:58,944 --> 00:37:59,945
Ho!

540
00:38:03,699 --> 00:38:04,783
Ho!

541
00:38:06,118 --> 00:38:06,994
Ho!

542
00:38:07,119 --> 00:38:09,121
If you don't pay interest this month,

543
00:38:09,246 --> 00:38:11,164
you'll never see your son again.

544
00:38:12,958 --> 00:38:14,376
Then lend me another million won.

545
00:38:14,501 --> 00:38:15,460
What?

546
00:38:15,585 --> 00:38:18,588
You're taking my son as collateral anyway.

547
00:38:18,714 --> 00:38:20,841
Lend me one million… No, two million.

548
00:38:24,970 --> 00:38:28,306
Ho, Mom will come get you, okay?

549
00:38:30,726 --> 00:38:31,893
Lend it to me.

550
00:38:39,693 --> 00:38:41,486
I feel bad for you.

551
00:38:41,611 --> 00:38:43,447
For having a mom like that.

552
00:38:49,327 --> 00:38:50,245
A kid jumped out.

553
00:38:50,996 --> 00:38:53,123
-Are you okay?
-What the…

554
00:38:54,958 --> 00:38:57,210
This is so freaking annoying.

555
00:38:58,253 --> 00:38:59,171
Hey!

556
00:39:30,827 --> 00:39:32,871
You know Granny Yong-seon
from Busan, right?

557
00:39:34,414 --> 00:39:37,084
How do you know Ms. Yong-seon…

558
00:39:38,418 --> 00:39:39,961
MS. YONG-SEON FROM BUSAN

559
00:39:47,302 --> 00:39:48,303
Yes, ma'am.

560
00:39:49,346 --> 00:39:50,639
Yes.

561
00:39:51,389 --> 00:39:52,682
Sorry?

562
00:39:52,808 --> 00:39:54,017
Understood.

563
00:39:54,142 --> 00:39:55,852
I'll call you back.

564
00:39:59,272 --> 00:40:00,690
We'll pay off the debt.

565
00:40:01,483 --> 00:40:03,026
We'll pay monthly interest, too.

566
00:40:03,151 --> 00:40:03,985
But…

567
00:40:04,945 --> 00:40:08,031
we'll only pay the legal interest rate
along with the principal.

568
00:40:08,156 --> 00:40:09,366
Mi-do, get up.

569
00:40:11,243 --> 00:40:12,911
Stay out of this. Get up.

570
00:40:15,705 --> 00:40:18,750
So don't ever show up at his work
like this again.

571
00:40:19,584 --> 00:40:23,755
If… you come here and lay a finger on him,

572
00:40:24,881 --> 00:40:26,133
you're dead.

573
00:40:27,259 --> 00:40:29,469
I'll really kill you.

574
00:40:42,357 --> 00:40:43,316
Mi-do.

575
00:40:46,862 --> 00:40:47,946
Mi-do.

576
00:40:54,661 --> 00:40:55,912
I guess I anticipated this

577
00:40:56,037 --> 00:40:57,914
when I wrote a script
involving loan sharks.

578
00:41:00,542 --> 00:41:02,919
Wow, I had such great foresight.

579
00:41:04,671 --> 00:41:06,798
Even though the movie fell through,

580
00:41:06,923 --> 00:41:10,594
sending Granny Yong-seon
red ginseng every holiday paid off.

581
00:41:12,470 --> 00:41:13,597
Namgung.

582
00:41:14,931 --> 00:41:17,184
I'll work hard on my writing.

583
00:41:18,185 --> 00:41:21,146
I'll swallow my pride and debut.

584
00:41:21,855 --> 00:41:23,899
We can pay it off together, okay?

585
00:41:24,900 --> 00:41:27,152
Don't you dare get any crazy ideas.

586
00:41:27,819 --> 00:41:30,155
Don't even think about
selling your liver or something.

587
00:41:34,743 --> 00:41:36,786
I know why you delayed our marriage.

588
00:41:39,122 --> 00:41:40,957
You said we'd wait until I debuted.

589
00:41:41,082 --> 00:41:42,959
That was just an excuse.

590
00:41:44,252 --> 00:41:45,795
It was because of your mom.

591
00:41:47,130 --> 00:41:48,590
You thought you'd burden me.

592
00:41:50,008 --> 00:41:52,761
I actually knew everything.
I just pretended not to.

593
00:41:54,930 --> 00:41:56,306
Honestly,

594
00:41:57,515 --> 00:41:59,434
I was a little scared.

595
00:42:01,353 --> 00:42:02,812
But not anymore.

596
00:42:03,647 --> 00:42:06,399
I'm really not scared anymore.

597
00:42:09,361 --> 00:42:10,779
Don't say you're sorry.

598
00:42:11,446 --> 00:42:13,031
Don't say thank you, either.

599
00:42:13,949 --> 00:42:14,950
Just…

600
00:42:16,743 --> 00:42:17,911
don't say anything.

601
00:42:19,454 --> 00:42:20,705
Don't say anything.

602
00:42:50,193 --> 00:42:51,528
Let's go on a trip.

603
00:42:52,862 --> 00:42:54,072
A trip?

604
00:42:55,240 --> 00:42:56,074
Yes.

605
00:42:57,200 --> 00:42:58,410
Let's go to Taipei.

606
00:42:59,452 --> 00:43:00,870
It was great three years ago.

607
00:43:04,374 --> 00:43:07,043
Let's do all the sightseeing
we missed last time.

608
00:43:08,086 --> 00:43:08,962
Like…

609
00:43:09,754 --> 00:43:11,381
the Shilin Night Market.

610
00:43:13,842 --> 00:43:17,637
And the place from  Spirited Away.
What was it called?

611
00:43:17,762 --> 00:43:20,181
-Jiufen?
-Yes, let's go there, too.

612
00:43:21,266 --> 00:43:22,934
Can you get time off?

613
00:43:23,059 --> 00:43:24,269
You're busy at work.

614
00:43:26,062 --> 00:43:27,522
I'll make it happen.

615
00:43:30,191 --> 00:43:31,318
Let's go.

616
00:43:32,527 --> 00:43:34,154
Really.

617
00:44:00,513 --> 00:44:01,556
Hello?

618
00:44:01,681 --> 00:44:03,892
What? She answers this number?

619
00:44:05,477 --> 00:44:07,187
Wow, that hurts my pride.

620
00:44:10,273 --> 00:44:11,858
This is so annoying.

621
00:44:12,776 --> 00:44:13,902
Gosh…

622
00:44:14,027 --> 00:44:16,321
Come on, give it to me.

623
00:44:16,446 --> 00:44:17,530
Hello?

624
00:44:17,655 --> 00:44:19,532
Do you live at Hines Officetel?

625
00:44:19,657 --> 00:44:21,910
I think you need to come outside.

626
00:44:22,035 --> 00:44:22,869
Excuse me?

627
00:44:22,994 --> 00:44:24,954
I'm in front of Hines Officetel,

628
00:44:25,080 --> 00:44:26,289
and my passenger is drunk.

629
00:44:27,791 --> 00:44:28,875
Hello, I--

630
00:44:42,889 --> 00:44:45,266
-Are you the one who answered the call?
-I am.

631
00:44:45,392 --> 00:44:48,353
Why did it take you so long?
I called so many times.

632
00:44:49,062 --> 00:44:52,315
He must've lost his wallet.
He hasn't paid me yet.

633
00:44:53,525 --> 00:44:57,195
I'm sorry, but could you
take him back to where he was?

634
00:44:57,320 --> 00:44:58,696
I'll pay for a round trip.

635
00:44:58,822 --> 00:44:59,906
That's a problem.

636
00:45:00,031 --> 00:45:01,950
I accepted a call when we spoke.

637
00:45:02,075 --> 00:45:04,202
If I cancel it now, I'll get a penalty.

638
00:45:07,122 --> 00:45:09,749
You can wire it to my account.
It's 35,000 won.

639
00:45:09,874 --> 00:45:12,252
Oh, okay. Just a second.

640
00:45:17,090 --> 00:45:18,299
I sent it.

641
00:45:18,425 --> 00:45:19,467
Lee Mi-do, right?

642
00:45:19,592 --> 00:45:20,552
-Yes.
-It went through.

643
00:45:20,677 --> 00:45:21,886
-Take care.
-You too.

644
00:46:00,175 --> 00:46:02,218
Just so you don't get the wrong idea,

645
00:46:02,927 --> 00:46:06,556
I'm only doing this
because I hate you being in my space.

646
00:46:09,350 --> 00:46:11,561
What the hell am I doing at this hour?

647
00:46:34,959 --> 00:46:36,002
Jeez.

648
00:47:02,779 --> 00:47:03,738
What?

649
00:47:04,864 --> 00:47:06,574
It really is Lee Mi-do.

650
00:47:07,742 --> 00:47:11,246
Mr. Han, you're very drunk.
We can talk later.

651
00:47:15,083 --> 00:47:16,417
Later when?

652
00:47:17,126 --> 00:47:18,920
You blocked my number.

653
00:47:22,131 --> 00:47:24,259
I have a lot of pride, you know?

654
00:47:25,218 --> 00:47:27,762
I'd never call you

655
00:47:28,763 --> 00:47:30,598
using someone else's phone.

656
00:47:31,849 --> 00:47:34,519
That's the best thing I've heard from you.

657
00:47:35,562 --> 00:47:38,189
Make sure you keep that promise.

658
00:47:43,945 --> 00:47:46,030
This is annoying.

659
00:47:47,198 --> 00:47:49,075
You're not my type.

660
00:47:52,579 --> 00:47:54,956
I don't even like older women.

661
00:48:02,964 --> 00:48:03,881
What?

662
00:48:06,175 --> 00:48:07,051
I'm telling you,

663
00:48:08,052 --> 00:48:10,054
you're not my type.

664
00:48:17,604 --> 00:48:18,479
Okay.

665
00:48:20,023 --> 00:48:21,232
I admit you're cute.

666
00:48:22,734 --> 00:48:23,735
No, no.

667
00:48:26,237 --> 00:48:29,157
I admit you're really cute.

668
00:48:33,369 --> 00:48:34,829
No.

669
00:48:36,914 --> 00:48:38,791
You're not cute at all.

670
00:48:41,878 --> 00:48:43,171
This is so annoying.

671
00:48:53,264 --> 00:48:54,223
Don't laugh at me.

672
00:48:58,227 --> 00:48:59,771
No, do it again.

673
00:49:09,447 --> 00:49:10,531
Mr. Han.

674
00:49:11,699 --> 00:49:12,659
It's just that

675
00:49:13,284 --> 00:49:16,037
you've never met a crazy bitch like me,

676
00:49:16,954 --> 00:49:18,748
so you're just confused.

677
00:49:19,749 --> 00:49:21,459
In a few days,

678
00:49:21,584 --> 00:49:26,297
you'll just think,
"Oh, there was that crazy bitch,"

679
00:49:27,590 --> 00:49:29,467
and you'll forget my face.

680
00:49:30,385 --> 00:49:31,427
So,

681
00:49:33,137 --> 00:49:34,847
just pretend you had cheap booze

682
00:49:36,265 --> 00:49:38,810
and got a bad stomachache,

683
00:49:42,188 --> 00:49:43,314
and forget about it.

684
00:49:47,110 --> 00:49:48,736
Want me to tell you a secret?

685
00:49:52,407 --> 00:49:53,950
I'm getting dumped soon.

686
00:50:04,127 --> 00:50:05,420
Go ahead and laugh.

687
00:50:06,254 --> 00:50:07,547
It's pretty funny.

688
00:50:16,973 --> 00:50:18,307
I missed you.

689
00:50:21,227 --> 00:50:22,311
You just kept…

690
00:50:24,021 --> 00:50:25,231
driving me crazy.

691
00:50:27,859 --> 00:50:29,318
I kept…

692
00:50:31,070 --> 00:50:32,071
and kept…

693
00:50:35,658 --> 00:50:36,784
Just kept…

694
00:50:40,705 --> 00:50:41,581
Kept…

695
00:51:01,684 --> 00:51:02,977
I missed you.

696
00:51:05,855 --> 00:51:07,106
You just kept…

697
00:51:50,691 --> 00:51:52,235
Good morning!

698
00:51:52,360 --> 00:51:53,361
Morning.

699
00:51:53,861 --> 00:51:54,904
MANAGER EOM HO-SIK

700
00:51:55,029 --> 00:51:57,114
-Good morning.
-Hey.

701
00:51:58,491 --> 00:51:59,951
All right…

702
00:52:02,703 --> 00:52:03,538
Can we talk?

703
00:52:15,091 --> 00:52:16,968
About the incident in the lobby yesterday,

704
00:52:17,885 --> 00:52:19,345
I took care of it myself.

705
00:52:21,722 --> 00:52:23,891
If HR Manager Jeong glares at you,

706
00:52:24,016 --> 00:52:25,560
just ignore him and move on.

707
00:52:26,477 --> 00:52:27,562
Wait, what?

708
00:52:28,396 --> 00:52:30,481
Did you plead with him for me?

709
00:52:31,440 --> 00:52:33,651
And about those posts
on the company intranet,

710
00:52:34,402 --> 00:52:36,529
they agreed to delete them right away.

711
00:52:36,654 --> 00:52:38,781
Best not to look. Stay off it for now.

712
00:52:40,032 --> 00:52:42,410
Don't tell me
you talked to Manager Shin from DX.

713
00:52:42,535 --> 00:52:44,412
Plus, under current company rules,

714
00:52:44,537 --> 00:52:46,163
they can't garnish your wages.

715
00:52:47,290 --> 00:52:50,209
So don't worry too much about that.

716
00:52:50,334 --> 00:52:52,587
Wow, even Finance Manager Yeom?

717
00:52:54,839 --> 00:52:56,007
Are you okay?

718
00:52:56,132 --> 00:52:58,092
Need anything else?

719
00:52:58,217 --> 00:52:59,844
I want the Paris posting.

720
00:53:02,638 --> 00:53:05,016
I know my chances are ruined
because of this incident.

721
00:53:06,142 --> 00:53:09,437
But if you beg
General Manager Kang, who knows?

722
00:53:09,562 --> 00:53:11,188
Since you're already begging,

723
00:53:11,314 --> 00:53:13,274
push a little harder for me.

724
00:53:13,399 --> 00:53:14,817
Tell them I really want to go.

725
00:53:14,942 --> 00:53:17,069
I'll swat you all the way to Paris!

726
00:53:20,197 --> 00:53:21,657
I'm just joking.

727
00:53:21,782 --> 00:53:23,117
Hey, do you know

728
00:53:23,242 --> 00:53:25,328
what I went through
because of you yesterday?

729
00:53:25,453 --> 00:53:27,330
I love you. Thank you.

730
00:53:28,122 --> 00:53:29,832
Without you, I'd be dragged to HR

731
00:53:29,957 --> 00:53:31,334
and sent to the Cheonan factory.

732
00:53:31,459 --> 00:53:34,754
I'm nothing without my suit.
That was close.

733
00:53:34,879 --> 00:53:36,964
What do you mean, "That was close"?

734
00:53:37,089 --> 00:53:39,675
Hey, just get lost, will you?

735
00:53:40,468 --> 00:53:42,637
Why do I even bother talking to you?

736
00:53:42,762 --> 00:53:43,763
Gosh.

737
00:53:43,888 --> 00:53:45,848
Speaking of which,

738
00:53:47,391 --> 00:53:49,518
you're approving my six-day leave
starting tomorrow, right?

739
00:53:49,644 --> 00:53:51,812
I asked days ago. Why no approval yet?

740
00:53:51,938 --> 00:53:54,523
I already bought my plane tickets.
Come on, please hurry.

741
00:53:54,649 --> 00:53:55,775
Hey!

742
00:53:56,525 --> 00:53:58,319
Are you some travel vlogger?

743
00:53:58,444 --> 00:54:00,696
What kind of bullshit are you spouting?

744
00:54:02,239 --> 00:54:03,407
That guy…

745
00:54:04,742 --> 00:54:06,118
LOVE EAT

746
00:54:07,495 --> 00:54:09,246
Where did Pudgy go?

747
00:54:10,873 --> 00:54:12,291
Did she get taken?

748
00:54:12,416 --> 00:54:13,960
Bambi was hospitalized.

749
00:54:14,669 --> 00:54:16,253
She has the herpes virus.

750
00:54:16,379 --> 00:54:17,588
It's common for cats.

751
00:54:17,713 --> 00:54:19,507
Anyway, she's at the vet.

752
00:54:25,179 --> 00:54:26,055
Is it bad?

753
00:54:26,722 --> 00:54:27,723
It was at first.

754
00:54:29,475 --> 00:54:31,560
But she's fine now. She's eating well.

755
00:54:32,353 --> 00:54:34,146
Get her spayed while she's there.

756
00:54:36,899 --> 00:54:39,527
Is that really all you have to say to me?

757
00:54:39,652 --> 00:54:41,195
I'll be off for six days.

758
00:54:43,280 --> 00:54:45,199
Don't be late on the seasoning mix report.

759
00:54:45,324 --> 00:54:46,242
I'll check with Sang-hun.

760
00:54:49,453 --> 00:54:51,372
I'll help you get that Paris posting.

761
00:54:56,293 --> 00:54:57,128
What?

762
00:54:57,253 --> 00:55:01,173
I looked into who's testing the waters
for the expat position.

763
00:55:01,298 --> 00:55:03,551
Your experience and qualifications
are far superior.

764
00:55:03,676 --> 00:55:04,552
So?

765
00:55:04,677 --> 00:55:07,596
I'll make sure
you're fully prepared for the interview.

766
00:55:08,514 --> 00:55:11,017
The person who went to Germany
was my mentor…

767
00:55:12,101 --> 00:55:13,060
Why not?

768
00:55:13,769 --> 00:55:15,771
You wanted to go to Paris.

769
00:55:15,896 --> 00:55:18,190
Ms. Ko got in by acing her interview.

770
00:55:18,899 --> 00:55:19,984
Ko Yun-jae?

771
00:55:20,818 --> 00:55:22,737
Her husband
is Director Im's wife's nephew.

772
00:55:23,404 --> 00:55:24,321
Sorry?

773
00:55:26,699 --> 00:55:29,285
Just figuring that out,
my naive little junior?

774
00:55:30,494 --> 00:55:31,620
Jeez.

775
00:55:34,206 --> 00:55:36,917
I never even dreamed
of getting the Paris position anyway.

776
00:55:39,086 --> 00:55:39,962
I just want

777
00:55:41,172 --> 00:55:42,965
the launch next year to be successful

778
00:55:43,632 --> 00:55:45,760
so I get a bonus… Hey, why the tears?

779
00:55:45,885 --> 00:55:47,803
I really wanted you to go.

780
00:55:49,263 --> 00:55:50,097
Why are you--

781
00:55:50,222 --> 00:55:51,265
I really…

782
00:55:52,641 --> 00:55:54,935
I really wanted to help you go.

783
00:55:56,645 --> 00:55:57,605
Hey, don't cry…

784
00:55:58,647 --> 00:55:59,607
Come on.

785
00:56:05,529 --> 00:56:06,655
Everyone's staring.

786
00:56:08,074 --> 00:56:10,159
Let's go over there.

787
00:56:16,332 --> 00:56:17,708
Are you looking for something?

788
00:56:18,334 --> 00:56:21,212
I need a gift for my boyfriend.

789
00:56:24,882 --> 00:56:27,510
Something long-lasting that won't wilt.

790
00:56:27,635 --> 00:56:30,888
Long-lasting? A dwarf umbrella tree.

791
00:56:31,013 --> 00:56:33,224
It symbolizes luck and prosperity,
so it makes a great gift.

792
00:56:33,349 --> 00:56:34,225
DWARF UMBRELLA TREE

793
00:56:34,350 --> 00:56:37,311
And the green color is calming,
so it's good for stress, too.

794
00:56:37,436 --> 00:56:40,523
It's nice and shiny, right?

795
00:56:40,648 --> 00:56:41,857
Will it last forever?

796
00:56:41,982 --> 00:56:44,819
Of course.
It grows well in the shade, too.

797
00:56:44,944 --> 00:56:47,571
With good care, it'll last a long time.

798
00:56:47,696 --> 00:56:48,697
I'll take it.

799
00:56:48,823 --> 00:56:50,241
Wow, that was fast.

800
00:56:52,326 --> 00:56:55,371
To celebrate our opening,
customers who spend over 80,000 won

801
00:56:55,496 --> 00:56:57,289
get a free gift.

802
00:57:00,668 --> 00:57:01,794
Thank you.

803
00:57:01,919 --> 00:57:03,838
Depending on the ball's color,

804
00:57:03,963 --> 00:57:07,466
you win a chrysanthemum,
plant food, or a saucer.

805
00:57:09,218 --> 00:57:10,886
Do I just press this button?

806
00:57:11,011 --> 00:57:12,680
Yes, just press the button.

807
00:57:24,233 --> 00:57:25,734
Damn it.

808
00:57:30,156 --> 00:57:31,574
Are you crazy?

809
00:57:41,250 --> 00:57:42,084
What's this?

810
00:57:43,627 --> 00:57:44,587
A voice recorder.

811
00:57:46,797 --> 00:57:49,008
I'll give you some plant food.

812
00:58:05,482 --> 00:58:06,442
Ma'am!

813
00:58:09,278 --> 00:58:11,655
I just spoke with
the detective in charge of Ms. Choi.

814
00:58:11,780 --> 00:58:16,035
Ms. Choi stated that Ms. Lee
helped fund the fraud for two years.

815
00:58:16,702 --> 00:58:20,456
You said you recorded
your last meeting with Ms. Choi.

816
00:58:20,581 --> 00:58:22,541
Can you send me that file?

817
00:58:22,666 --> 00:58:23,918
Yes, I'll send it now.

818
00:58:43,729 --> 00:58:44,730
Oh, right.

819
00:58:45,522 --> 00:58:46,649
The laptop's broken.

820
00:58:47,524 --> 00:58:48,359
Damn it…

821
00:58:53,280 --> 00:58:56,116
MIDORI

822
00:59:36,865 --> 00:59:38,993
Do you know what you just did?

823
00:59:46,417 --> 00:59:49,420
Oh, come on.

824
00:59:51,714 --> 00:59:53,424
You don't want to direct, do you?

825
00:59:54,258 --> 00:59:55,426
You're scared, aren't you?

826
00:59:56,427 --> 00:59:57,511
I WAS SO IMPRESSED

827
00:59:57,678 --> 00:59:59,221
INDIE FILM'S NEW HOPE
A FAN AS OF TODAY

828
00:59:59,388 --> 01:00:02,308
LEE MI-DO IS THE BEST

829
01:00:02,474 --> 01:00:04,476
I knew it. You're scared.

830
01:00:05,269 --> 01:00:06,103
No, I'm not.

831
01:00:06,228 --> 01:00:07,271
THE LINES DELIVER THE STORY

832
01:00:07,396 --> 01:00:08,397
That's not it.

833
01:00:09,857 --> 01:00:10,983
Yes, you are.

834
01:00:11,900 --> 01:00:12,776
You want to run away.

835
01:00:12,901 --> 01:00:13,819
WHAT IS A MOVIE?

836
01:00:13,944 --> 01:00:15,696
You're scared and terrified.

837
01:00:16,613 --> 01:00:18,240
I LIKED THE ENDING WHEN THEY PART
I LOOK FORWARD TO YOUR NEXT PROJECT

838
01:00:18,490 --> 01:00:20,034
But you feel bad for your boyfriend,

839
01:00:20,701 --> 01:00:22,286
so you're too ashamed to do it.

840
01:00:23,787 --> 01:00:24,621
Am I wrong?

841
01:00:26,290 --> 01:00:27,291
You're wrong.

842
01:00:34,590 --> 01:00:36,216
Want me to help you escape?

843
01:00:38,677 --> 01:00:41,722
You were desperate enough
to go beg Song Hae-na,

844
01:00:43,599 --> 01:00:45,684
but I got in the way and ruined it.

845
01:00:47,394 --> 01:00:51,774
You can say you had the talent
but just got unlucky.

846
01:00:56,320 --> 01:00:58,572
You got tangled up with some crazy guy,

847
01:00:59,656 --> 01:01:01,408
and got completely screwed over.

848
01:01:05,162 --> 01:01:08,332
Burying a rookie director
before they even start

849
01:01:08,999 --> 01:01:11,085
is incredibly easy for me.

850
01:01:13,379 --> 01:01:15,756
Why would you go that far for me?

851
01:01:16,924 --> 01:01:18,675
What do you want from me?

852
01:01:20,511 --> 01:01:21,720
One thing is for sure.

853
01:01:23,180 --> 01:01:24,681
It's not because of the settlement.

854
01:02:32,249 --> 01:02:37,129
DWARF UMBRELLA TREE

855
01:02:37,796 --> 01:02:39,631
You said nothing happened.

856
01:02:39,756 --> 01:02:41,216
That I had nothing to worry about.

857
01:02:41,341 --> 01:02:43,218
I'll just disappear from your life.

858
01:02:43,343 --> 01:02:45,721
I said I'll get out of your life!

859
01:02:45,846 --> 01:02:47,723
What is your problem?

860
01:02:47,848 --> 01:02:49,600
I'm terrible, aren't I?

861
01:02:49,725 --> 01:02:51,059
You must be disappointed.

862
01:02:51,643 --> 01:02:53,729
Ms. Lee and I aren't like that.

863
01:02:53,854 --> 01:02:55,105
Not buying it?

864
01:02:55,230 --> 01:02:57,483
I know everything I say will be an excuse.

865
01:02:57,608 --> 01:03:01,153
Just how miserable do you want to make me?

866
01:03:02,488 --> 01:03:03,322
Mi-do.

867
01:03:03,447 --> 01:03:05,782
Listen carefully to what I'm about to say.

868
01:03:06,450 --> 01:03:08,410
Subtitle Translation by Cayle Kim
